      "degree_level": "Bachelor, Master",
      "process_description": "Eligible students must have relevant prior coursework passed for the chosen research area; consult the table’s \"Remarks\" column for specific prerequisites. To obtain a supervisor you either (A) propose your own topic by submitting a 2–3 page Research Proposal via the Business Theses Market, or (B) apply for a listed topic on the Market with CV, current transcript (export from module booking) and a short motivational letter. Use your UZH login to apply. Matching may take up to two months; successful matches lead to contact by the supervisor and the final assignment is posted on OLAT. Picking up the assignment on OLAT starts the fixed six‑month work period; submit the thesis and attachments as a ZIP on OLAT. Grades arrive within one month. Follow Dekanat (Studium und Abschluss) rules; the institute may require revisions or reject proposals.",
